	<description>From the highly acclaimed, award-winning author of &lt;i&gt;Floating in My Mother's Palm&lt;/i&gt; comes a stunning novel about ordinary people living in extraordinary times.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Trudi Montag is a &lt;i&gt;Zwerg&lt;/i&gt;—a dwarf—short, undesirable, different, the voice of anyone who has ever tried to fit in. Eventually she learns that being different is a secret that all humans share—from her mother who flees into madness, to her friend Georg whose parents pretend he's a girl, to the Jews Trudy harbors in her cellar.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Ursula Hegi brings us a timeless and unforgettable story in Trudi and a small town, weaving together a profound tapestry of emotional power, humanity, and truth.</description>
